00:53:06.430 --> 00:53:19.570
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The judge gives permission to cuss. And Dr. Hill, who had prepared nothing, has nothing written down, begins repeating the messages verbatim. It's like she's been waiting to let them out.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>法官准许骂人。Hill博士，什么都没准备，没有写下任何东西，开始逐字重复留言。就像她一直等着把它们发泄出来。

00:53:19.570 --> 00:53:32.540
<v Teresa Hill>I was called a fucking cunt. I was told to sit and spin on a sandpaper dildo. I was told to disappear. I was told to eat the end of a shotgun.
<v Teresa Hill>我被骂是个该死的妓女。我被告知坐上去在磨砂膏假阳具上转。我被告知消失。我被告知吃下猎枪的枪口。

00:53:32.540 --> 00:53:53.230
<v Teresa Hill>I was told not to go out in public. I was told, we're not coming to the school, we're coming to your house. And I lived in fear for four months after that.
<v Teresa Hill>我被告知不要公开露面。我被告知，我们不来学校，我们来你家。在那之后，我在恐惧中生活了四个月。

00:53:53.230 --> 00:54:17.990
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>A friend of mine, an assistant principal for decades now, told me he still remembers his mentor explaining early on that the job of a school leader is never inflict pain on an institution. The job is to absorb pain for the institution. It must be confusing to be any kind of public official right now, trying to absorb the pain of the last few years.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我的一个朋友，一位当了几十年副校长的朋友，告诉我他仍然记得他的导师在早期解释说，学校领导的工作从来不是给机构造成痛苦。工作是为机构吸收痛苦。现在做任何类型的公职人员一定很困惑，试图吸收过去几年的痛苦。

00:54:17.990 --> 00:54:50.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>How many principals or election officials or public health officials or prime ministers of countries have scrambled to respond to a public that is rageful by doing what they know how to do, by throwing PowerPoints at people, by holding public hearings, printing out color charts, only to finally understand that all the vitriol and misinformation was always going to be too enormous for any one person to absorb. Principal Hill shielded everyone else from distress until it was only hers.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>有多少校长、选举官员、公共卫生官员或国家总理为了回应愤怒的公众，通过做他们知道怎么做的事情，通过向人们扔PPT，通过举行公开听证会，打印彩色图表，却最终发现所有的愤怒和错误信息对于任何一个人来说都太大而无法吸收。Hill校长保护了其他人免受困扰，直到它变成了她一个人的困扰。

00:54:50.770 --> 00:55:06.620
<v Teresa Hill>But it wasn't just the words. It was the isolation that I felt with it. I felt like I was all alone in dealing with the situation. That is what made me say, I can't do this anymore.
<v Teresa Hill>但这不仅仅是言语。这是我感受到的孤独感。我觉得在处理这种情况下我孤身一人。这就是让我说，我不能再这样做了的原因。

00:55:06.620 --> 00:55:10.690
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So many of these voicemails are asking for you to resign.
